/**
 * Hand-written tool descriptions.
 *
 * `tools.ts` used to generate both locales from a template, producing English like
 * "Measure with Word Counter in a focused browser workbench." for all 283 tools — one
 * of nine stock verbs, the tool's own name, and a sentence about privacy repeated
 * verbatim on every card. The Bangla side was a single sentence with the English tool
 * name interpolated into it. Every card read the same, several read ungrammatically
 * ("Work with Basic Auth Header"), and none of them said what the tool actually does.
 *
 * These are keyed by tool name, which is already the source of truth for the slug.
 * A name with no entry here falls back to the old template rather than rendering
 * empty, so the map can be incomplete without breaking a page. `scripts/i18n-parity.mjs`
 * reports how many tools are still on the fallback.
 *
 * Descriptions are one sentence, say what the tool does rather than restating its
 * name, and leave the shared privacy promise to the page chrome instead of repeating
 * it 283 times.
 */
